# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.DS_Store

# Local agent-tool config that isn't shared (graft's cache is at the bottom,
# with the note on why ripgrep still sees it).
.mcp.json
GEMINI.md
# graft's per-machine install. Its helpers bake an absolute path into the
# installer's node_modules, and its .claude/settings.json registers hooks on
# every session, prompt, tool call and stop — committed, both would break or
# fail for anyone without graft. The rest only point at the (also ignored)
# graft/ cache. Named precisely, so a genuinely shared file in these
# directories can still be committed on purpose.
.claude/settings.json
.claude/helpers/
.claude/skills/graft/
.agents/skills/graft/
.github/copilot-instructions.md
.ignore

# Runtime-mutable state produced by the loop.
# runtime/target.py is the committed naive baseline; the loop overwrites it
# at runtime, but we keep the pristine version under version control.
runtime/target.py.bak
runtime/episodic.jsonl
runtime/episodic_state.json
runtime/episodic.duckdb
# Who changed which config key, when, and why (OMNI-28) — a local operational
# record of this machine's console, not source.
runtime/operator_audit.jsonl
# Drafted contracts awaiting human approval — local review state, not source.
runtime/contract_staging/

# Editor / tooling
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude-code-gui/

# Terraform (infra/aws). State records resource attributes and terraform.tfvars
# holds the alert email; neither belongs in a public repo. The .terraform.lock.hcl
# provider lock IS committed, by Terraform convention.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform/
terraform.tfvars

# Secrets (see DESIGN.md §6). Local dev only — never commit real credentials.
# secrets.example.yml IS committed (template); secrets.local.yml is NOT.
.env
secrets.local.yml
*.local.yml
secrets/
!secrets.example.yml

# graft's local graph cache — regenerable, not committed (run `graft build`).
/graft/
